  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="a27c-bf11-0b7f-8125" name="Carthaginian (Hannibal) - List Notes" publicationId="fc9f-8438-629b-e92d" hidden="false">
      <description>CARTHAGINIAN ARMY LIST (Hannibal &amp; the Punic Wars, pp.20-27)
Characters up to 25% of points; at least one character must be the Army General. Common and Uncommon Troop limits and membership depend on the chosen war (force entry). "R:" means restricted: at least one unit of the listed type must be taken first (not enforced).
Mercenary Army General: only in the First Punic War, and optionally elsewhere as listed in the unit entry.
ALLIES (p.26; not enforced): Gallic, Sicilian Greek, Syracusan, Campanian/Bruttian/Lucanian, Samnite, Spanish, Numidian. Allies do not gain the benefit of the Army General or other Carthaginian characters.
OPTIONAL RULES (p.27): Pikes, Un-Crewed Elephants, Mercenaries, Fortified Camp (with opponent permission).
Mounted models may ride a horse (M8, free) or a Warhorse (M8 WS3 BS0 S3 I3 A1). All bows are composite bows with range 24".

ARMY COMPOSITIONS:
[Carthaginian - First Punic War]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Troops: at least 50%
  Uncommon Troops: up to 33%
  Common: Levy Africans; Mercenary Hoplites; Gallic Warriors (R: Mercenary Hoplites); Spanish Infantry (R: Mercenary Hoplites); Skirmishers; Numidian Cavalry (R: Punic Heavy Cavalry).
  Uncommon: Peltasts and Thureophoroi (R: Mercenary Hoplites); Punic Heavy Cavalry; Campanian Cavalry (R: Mercenary Hoplites); Elephants; Balearic Slingers; Ligurian Infantry; Sardinian Archers; Artillery.
[Carthaginian - Second Punic War in Spain]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Troops: at least 50%
  Uncommon Troops: up to 25%
  The Army General may not be a Mercenary General.
  Common: Trained Africans; Gallic Warriors; Spanish Infantry; Skirmishers; Numidian Cavalry (R: Trained Africans); Celtiberian Scutarii (R: Spanish Infantry).
  Uncommon: Spanish Cavalry; Gallic Cavalry; Elephants (R: Trained Africans); Balearic Slingers; Artillery.
[Carthaginian - Second Punic War in Italy]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Troops: at least 50%
  Uncommon Troops: up to 33%
  The Army General may not be a Mercenary General.
  Common: Trained Africans; Veterans; Oscan Infantry; Italian Infantry; Gallic Warriors (R: Trained Africans, Veterans); Gallic Veterans (R: Trained Africans, Veterans); Spanish Infantry (R: Trained Africans, Veterans); Skirmishers; Numidian Cavalry (R: Trained Africans, Veterans, Oscan Infantry, Italian Infantry).
  Uncommon: Campanian Cavalry (R: Oscan Infantry, Italian Infantry); Spanish Cavalry; Gallic Cavalry; Elephants (R: only one, and only with Trained Africans, Veterans); Balearic Slingers; Celtiberian Scutarii (R: Trained Africans, Veterans); Roman Deserters; Ligurian Infantry; Artillery.
[Carthaginian - Second Punic War in Africa]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Troops: at least 50%
  Uncommon Troops: up to 33%
  The Army General may not be a Mercenary General.
  Common: Citizens; Trained Africans; Levy Africans (R: Citizens); Veterans; Oscan Infantry; Bruttian Veterans (R: Veterans); Skirmishers; Numidian Cavalry (R: Trained Africans, Levy Africans, Veterans); Punic Heavy Cavalry .
  Uncommon: Spanish Cavalry (R: Trained Africans, Veterans); Gallic Cavalry (R: Trained Africans, Veterans); Elephants; Balearic Slingers; Celtiberian Scutarii (R: Trained Africans, Veterans); Ligurian Infantry; Moorish Archers; Artillery.
[Carthaginian - Third Punic War in Africa]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Troops: at least 75%
  Uncommon Troops: up to 25%
  The Army General may not be a Mercenary General.
  Common: Citizens; Trained Africans; Levy Africans; Skirmishers; Numidian Cavalry (R: Trained Africans, Levy Africans).
  Uncommon: Punic Heavy Cavalry; Artillery.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
